        <mxCell id="legend" value="NOTATION (Unit 1 slides): Rectangle = entity; diamond = relationship; oval = attribute; underline = candidate key.&lt;br/&gt;Min–max labels are placed on the participating entity’s line: (0,N) optional many; (0,1) optional one; (1,1) exactly one / total participation.&lt;br/&gt;Foreign keys are introduced during ER-to-relational mapping, not repeated as conceptual ER attributes.&lt;br/&gt;RECEIVES: USERS plays the assignee role (STAFF). CREATES: USERS plays the assigning actor role (ADMIN). RECORDS: USERS plays the actor role.&lt;br/&gt;Each complaint has at most one feedback record and one current embedding. Feedback and embeddings have independent surrogate IDs.&lt;br/&gt;A complaint may initially have no status log in the structural model; application transactions must create the initial log on submission.&lt;br/&gt;Vector is a single vector-valued attribute handled by pgvector, not a multivalued attribute requiring a double oval." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=17;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#222222;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;fontSize=19;fillColor=#f5f5f5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="100" y="2630" width="4080" height="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
