        <mxCell id="notes" value="MAPPING AND CONSTRAINTS&lt;br/&gt;1:N relationships: copy the key on the 1-side into the relation on the N-side (foreign keys shown by arrows).&lt;br/&gt;1:1 optional extensions: FEEDBACK.complaint_id and COMPLAINT_EMBEDDINGS.complaint_id are NOT NULL + UNIQUE foreign keys.&lt;br/&gt;Candidate keys: ROLES(role_name), USERS(email), DEPARTMENTS(department_name), CATEGORIES(department_id, category_name). Only primary keys are underlined here.&lt;br/&gt;All foreign keys are NOT NULL. Optional attributes: COMPLAINTS.resolved_at; ASSIGNMENTS.ended_at; STATUS_HISTORY.old_status and remarks; FEEDBACK.comment.&lt;br/&gt;Domains: priority ∈ {LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, URGENT}; status ∈ {SUBMITTED, ASSIGNED, IN_PROGRESS, RESOLVED, REJECTED}; rating ∈ [1,5]; target_hours &amp;gt; 0.&lt;br/&gt;At most one active assignment per complaint: UNIQUE(complaint_id) WHERE ended_at IS NULL. Ended assignments remain as history.&lt;br/&gt;Resolution time: resolved_at is present iff status = RESOLVED; resolved_at ≥ created_at. ended_at ≥ assigned_at when present.&lt;br/&gt;Semantic rules enforced by transactions / triggers: role permissions, valid transitions, current-status/history consistency, and feedback by the reporter only after resolution.&lt;br/&gt;pgvector extension: embedding VECTOR(384), fixed 384-dimensional model, cosine retrieval; content_hash detects stale text embeddings.&lt;br/&gt;Department is obtained through COMPLAINTS → CATEGORIES → DEPARTMENTS; no redundant department_id in COMPLAINTS.&lt;br/&gt;Design refinement: feedback_id and embedding_id are surrogate PKs; UNIQUE complaint_id preserves the previous 0..1 cardinalities." style="html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=17;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#222222;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=18;fontSize=19;fillColor=#f5f5f5;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="70" y="1930" width="2680" height="450" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>